  "strings": {
    "PassionCode.ai | Open-source workplace for AI agents": "",
    "Build your own workplace for AI agents. Fabric, the CEO AI agent, keeps the project; your coding agent creates new agents and converts the ones you have; Fabric Dashboards, Switchboard and Project Observatory run and watch them. Open source and free.": "",
    "Create your workplace, create agents, convert the ones you have. Open source under the GNU AGPL-3.0 and free to use.": "",
    "PassionCode.ai — a toolkit for AI-native teams": "",
    "A toolkit for AI-native teams: Fabric, the CEO AI agent, its tools and the contracts that make any agent Fabric-compatible. Open source under the GNU AGPL-3.0, with a commercial license available.": "",
    "Is PassionCode.ai free?": "",
    "Yes. Every tool is open source under the GNU AGPL-3.0: you can download, use, study and change it at no cost. A commercial license is available when you ship it inside a closed product or run a modified hosted service without publishing its source.": "",
    "Which agents does it work with?": "",
    "It is agent-agnostic. Claude Code and Codex are supported today; any agent, MCP server or command-line tool can become a Fabric-compatible service with the Fabric Agent Adapter.": "",
    "How do I turn an existing project or agent into a Fabric agent?": "",
    "Install the PassionCode.ai launcher (npx @passioncode-ai/passioncode@latest update), then ask your coding agent to adapt the project to Fabric. The Fabric Agent Adapter skill wraps it as a service with a contract, a dashboard and a conformance check.": "",
    "Can PassionCode.ai set this up for my company?": "",
    "Yes. Describe your team and processes on passioncode.ai/business/ and we reply with an estimate and a proposal: guided onboarding, or a workplace we build and run for you.": "",
