    "Step-by-step guide": "",
    "Create agents": "",
    "Ask Claude Code or Codex for the agent you need: a release publisher, a support triager, a weekly report. The Fabric Agent Adapter skill builds it as a service with its own contract, dashboard and tests. Fabric will do this for you from a conversation; today your coding agent does it with the same skill.": "",
    "you": "",
    "Create a Fabric agent that drafts release notes from merged pull requests": "",
    "Convert what you already have": "",
    "An agent, an MCP server, a command-line tool or a whole project becomes a Fabric-compatible service without a rewrite. The conformance probe tells you what is missing.": "",
    "Adapt this repository to Fabric": "",
    "Run them and see everything": "",
    "Fabric Dashboards shows every service in one window and lets agents start and stop them. Switchboard picks the account each agent runs on. Project Observatory shows what changed in every project, with evidence.": "",
    "Choose the tools": "",
    "Yours, all the way down.": "",
    "Everything runs on your machines and your accounts. Every line is public on GitHub under the GNU AGPL-3.0. No sign-up, no fee, no lock-in to one model or vendor.": "",
